          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Since generally an
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equation"} equation
            is the statement of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality"} equality
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi(x) = \psi(y)
            of two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ψ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variables"} variables
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            %em linear equation
            is an equation between
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+functions"} linear functions
          %h3#in_1category_theory In 1-category theory
          %p
            Typically here a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+function"} linear function
            is taken to mean an
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              \-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear map
            over some given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : X \to Z
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo :
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi : Y \to Z
            of (say left)
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Z
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X, Y, Z \in R
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mod"} Mod
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
            is an
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rank"} rank
            greater than 1, one also speaks of a
            = succeed "." do
              %em system of linear equations
          %p
            Specifically if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo =
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R = k
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            then these are linear maps of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
            and hence in this case a linear equation is a statement of equality of two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vectors"} vectors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi(x) = \psi(y)
            in some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
            that depend linearly on vectors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            in a vector spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in Y
          %p
            Frequently this is considered specifically for the case that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ψ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+function"} constant function
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector"} vector
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi(x) = g
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            here is represented or representable by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrix"} matrix
            this is typically written as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mover
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                  %mo =
                  %mover
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\phi \cdot\vec x = \vec g
                  \\,,
          %p
            which is the form that one finds in standard textbooks on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+algebra"} linear algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vec g = 0
            here this is called a
            = succeed "." do
              %em homogeneous linear equation
          %p
            But linear equations make sense and are important in the greater generality where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is not necessarily a field, and in fact in contexts more general than that of
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphisms"} natural isomorphisms
            between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+functors"} linear functors
            are a kind of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorification"} categorification
            of linear equations.
          %h3#in_category_theory
            In
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            Indeed, as discussed at
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equation"} equation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+logic"} formal logic
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            a an equation as above is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/judgement"} judgement
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo :
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi Type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  x : X , y : Y \vdash (\phi(x) = \psi(y)) : Type
          %p
            whose solution space is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum"} dependent sum
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sol
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo ⊢
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo :
                          %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mi y
                          %mo :
                          %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi Type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Sol \;\; \coloneqq \vdash \sum_{{x : X} \atop {y : Y}} (\phi(x) = \psi(y)) : Type
          %p
            and reading this in fact in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            says that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Sol
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X, Y, Sol
            are
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
          %p
            The generalization of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            is an
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E-ring"} E-∞-ring
            and that of an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X, Y
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+spectrum"} module spectrum
          %p
            Accordingly a linear equation in
            = succeed "(" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} type
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            is a statement of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
            between elements of an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+spectrum"} module spectrum
            that depend
            = succeed "-linearly" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equation"} equation
            = succeed "-linear" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                          %msubsup
                            %mo ×
                            %mi Z
                            %mn ∞
                          %mi Y
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi Y
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⇙
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi ψ
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo →
                            %mi ϕ
                        %mtd
                          %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  X \times_Z^\infty Y &amp;\to&amp; Y
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;\swArrow&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\psi}}
                  \\\
                  X &amp;\underset{\phi}{\to}&amp; Z
                  }
          %p
            in an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-modules"} ∞-modules
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#solution_spaces_of_homogeneous_linear_equations
            Solution spaces of homogeneous
            = succeed "-linear" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %p
            We discuss solution space of homogeneous linear equations in the general context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+algebra"} linear algebra
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            (not necessarily a
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
          %p
            So let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N \in R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mod"} Mod
            be an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi n
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi n
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n_0,n_1 \in \mathbb{N}
            and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi K
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K = (K_{i j})
            be an an
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi n
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mi n
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n_0 \times n_1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrix"} matrix
            with entries in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrix+multiplication"} matrix multiplication
            this defines a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+function"} linear function
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi N
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi n
                        %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi N
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi n
                        %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  K \cdot (-) : N^{n_0} \to N^{n_1}
                  \\,.
          %p
            which takes the element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi u
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi u
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi n
                        %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi N
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi n
                        %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vec u = (u_1, \cdots, u_{n_0}) \in N^{n_0}
            to the element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mover
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \cdot \vec u
            with
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi K
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mover
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi i
                  %mo =
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi n
                        %mn 0
                  %msub
                    %mi K
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msub
                    %mi u
                    %mi j
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (K \cdot \vec u)_i = \sum_{j = 1}^{n_0} K_{i j}\cdot u_j
                  \\,.
          %p Consider dually the linear map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msup
                    %mi K
                    %mi T
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi n
                        %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi n
                        %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (-) \cdot K^T : R^{n_1} \to R^{n_0}
          %p
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+modules"} free modules
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %p
            Consider the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi n
                        %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R^{n_1}
            by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
            of this map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi n
                        %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi n
                        %mn 0
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msup
                    %mi K
                    %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  R^{n_1}/ (R^{n_0} \cdot K^T)
                  \\,,
          %p
            hence the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernel"} cokernel
            of the map, fitting in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequence"} exact sequence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi n
                        %mn 1
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi K
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi n
                        %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi n
                        %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi n
                        %mn 1
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msup
                    %mi K
                    %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  R^{n_1} \stackrel{(-)\cdot K}{\to} R^{n_0} \to R^{n_1}/(R^{n_1}\cdot K^T)
                  \\to 0
          %p
            Here the morphism on the left is also called the inclusion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/syzygies"} syzygies
            of the module on the right.
          %p
            Applying the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+exact+functor"} left exact
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom+functor"} hom functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mi Mod
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_{R Mod}(-,N)
            to this yields
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequence"} exact sequence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mi Mod
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi n
                        %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi n
                        %mn 0
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msup
                    %mi K
                    %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi N
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi n
                        %mn 0
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mi N
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi n
                        %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  0 \to Hom_{R Mod}(R^{n_1}/(R^{n_0}\cdot K^T), N)
                  \\to
                  N^{n_0}
                  \\stackrel{K \cdot(-)}{\to}
                  N^{n_1}
                  \\,.
          %p
            This identifies
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mi Mod
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi n
                        %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi n
                        %mn 0
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_{R Mod}(R^{n_1}/(R^{n_0}\cdot K), N)
            as the space of solutions of the
            %em homogeneous
            linear
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equation"} equation
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mover
                      %mi u
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \cdot \vec u = 0
          %p (…)
          %h3#relation_to_syzygies_and_projective_resolutions_of_modules Relation to syzygies and projective resolutions of modules
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                \-linear equations in finitely many variables;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generators+and+relations"} finitely generated
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/syzygies"} syzygies
                in these
                = succeed "-modules" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %li
              %p
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+resolutions"} projective resolutions
                of these
                = succeed "-modules." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %p These relations we discuss in the following.
          %p (…)
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
